[2026-09-27 14:25:14] [MODULE] Brand logo — Navbar and footer brand logo now render public/images/logo.png. Added an optional image prop to x-brand.logo (resources/views/components/brand/logo.blade.php) that switches from the BtA monogram badge to a circular cropped <img>; navbar and footer pass image="images/logo.png". The admin sidebar and auth pages still use the monogram. 18 PublicPagesTest tests pass.
[2026-09-27 14:25:14] [MODULE] Prompt logging — Prompt capture is now automatic and crash-proof. Added the opencode plugin .opencode/plugins/prompt-logger.js, which hooks chat.message and appends every user prompt to prompt.log and PROMPT_LOG.md at submit time, before the model runs, so prompts survive session close or navigating back. Handles de-duplication via messageID+text hash, multi-line prompts, and file attachments; wrapped in try/catch so logging can never break a session. Backfilled this session's three prompts. Added AGENTS.md instructing the agent to log only RESULT/MODULE entries via php artisan prompts:log and never re-write prompt blocks, so the automatic log cannot be duplicated.
[2026-09-27 14:30:50] [MODULE] Tab titles — Browser tab titles are now 'SECTION | Balai ti Arjud' across every section and feature, with admin pages keeping the trailing 'Admin'. The three layouts (customer, guest, admin) now render the title as {{ Str::upper(trim($__env->yieldContent('title', <default>))) }} | {{ config('app.name') }}, so upper-casing and the pipe separator are applied in one place and all 44 existing @section('title', ...) values keep writing natural casing. Defaults set to Home / Log In / Dashboard. Renamed the home section from 'Glow & Beauty Lounge' to 'Home' so the tab reads HOME. Added tests/Feature/TabTitleTest.php covering all nine public sections, a dynamic service-detail title, and the admin suffix.
[2026-09-27 14:35:59] [MODULE] Home page trim — Removed three sections from the home page only: the About Us section (id=about), the 'Inside the Lounge / Beautiful moments, captured' gallery section (id=gallery), and the 'Book Online' booking CTA card (id=booking). The hero and the Special Offers section (id=offers) remain, and the back-to-top button was kept. Also renamed the services index page title from 'Browse Services' to 'Services' so its tab reads SERVICES | Balai ti Arjud. Updated TabTitleTest to match. Verified no views or routes still reference the removed #about/#gallery/#booking anchors. Note: the home-about, home-gallery and home-cta CSS rules in resources/css/app.css are now unused.
[2026-09-27 14:39:19] [MODULE] Tab titles — Clicking the navbar Promo link now retitles the browser tab to 'PROMO | Balai ti Arjud'. Because the link is an in-page anchor to home#offers, no page load happens, so the server-rendered title would stay 'HOME'. Added initSectionTabTitles() to resources/js/app.js, a vanilla helper matching the existing initPasswordToggles pattern: links carrying data-tab-title set document.title on click, and a hashchange listener re-derives the title from the target section's own data-tab-title, restoring the page's original title when the hash is dropped. Both the desktop and mobile Promo links and the #offers section carry data-tab-title so click and hash change always agree. This also means a shared /#offers URL and back/forward navigation land on the right title. Added a TabTitleTest case asserting both markup halves.
[2026-09-27 14:43:07] [MODULE] Tab titles — Fixed a real bug in the Promo tab title: the title snapped straight back to HOME. Cause was that the live database has zero promos, so the #offers section is not rendered at all (it is behind an @if on active promos), and the hashchange handler fell back to the page title whenever its target element was missing - clobbering the title the click had just set. initSectionTabTitles() now records each data-tab-title link's claim for its own hash in a Map and uses that as the fallback, so the PROMO title survives whether or not the target section renders. Reported to the user that the offers section is empty in the live DB and that the Promo link has nothing to scroll to until promos are added.
[2026-09-27 14:46:41] [MODULE] Promo data — Seeded the demo promos into the live database at the user's request, because the Promo nav link had no section to scroll to. Ran only ContentSeeder (not DatabaseSeeder) so no other live data was touched; seedPromos() uses updateOrCreate on title so it is idempotent. Three promos inserted, one currently visible: 'Glow Package Discount' (2026-09-22 to 2026-10-22). 'Loyalty Week' does not start until 2026-10-07 and 'Mother's Day Special' is inactive and expired, so scopeActive's date window hides both. Cleared the promo banner cache and confirmed via curl on http://localhost/BTA/public/ that the #offers section, both Promo nav links and the footer banner now render.
[2026-09-27 14:55:13] [MODULE] Tab titles — Verified the Promo tab title end to end and fixed a second real bug. Because no headless browser is available, exercised the actual minified function out of public/build/assets against a stub DOM across 7 scenarios (fresh load, click, hashchange, back button, direct /#offers load, and the missing-section case). That exposed a flaw: titlesByHash was only populated inside the 'already bound' guard, so any re-init left the fallback map empty and hashchange reset the title to the page title. Moved the map population above the guard so the function is idempotent. Also confirmed there is no stale-bundle or cache problem - the served HTML references the current hash, Vite leaves exactly one bundle on disk, no PHP dev server is running so Apache is the only entry point, and response headers are no-cache.
